Not necessarily.  This may depend on your particular board type.  Which
one do you have?  In particular Nautilus support had bugs which could
cause disk corruption in right circumstances.  This particular one for
Nautilus was fixed in "ac" series (it was fixed and posted on this list
by Hyung Min Seo and I do not know yet if it is present in 2.4.3) and I
was running a patched kernel for ten days without any problems before
rebooting into something else for diffent type of tests.  In general a
number of fixes for Alpha went into "ac".

