On Wed, 4 Apr 2001, Rob Byrnes wrote:

> Does anyone have any experince with the Accton EN1207D-TX cards 
> (http://www.accton.com.sg/accton/products/adapters/en1207bcd/base.html) 
> ?  These are supposedly Digital chips, but I am unable to find out if they 
> use the Tulip chips or not.
> 
> Accton do provide a linux driver, but AFAICT, there is no mention of Tulip.

I think it's based on the SMC9332, which is supported by the de4x5
driver.  There are some notes in the de4x5 driver source in 2.4.x that
mention that the SMC9332 cards (and Accton, although it doesn't mention a
model #) have a broken SROM, so the driver attempts a fixup.  I'm not sure
how successful this might be on Alpha, though, since I didn't read the
code yet.  If it's not expensive (ie $25USD or less), it may be worthwhile
just to pick one up and test it out.  If it's not working correctly, I'm
sure the driver author(s) would appreciate some help in debugging it...

Anyone have any experience with the SMC9332?

C




