SlotB is expensive. That is why AMD bailed out of the Slot business and 
went to SocketA


> >
> > I believe there is no reason to go back in 164, no way... it is cheaper now
> > to create
> > UP1500 than 164 system.
>
>I believe there was no reason to leave EV56 to begin with. It's been 3-4
>years
>now and how much has the price come down on EV6? UP1100 cost 2K retail.
>UP1500 is
>rumored to cost the same . Availability of UP1100 has been a problem in
>the
>US and hence people didnt buy them. So you're still talking 3K for a
>complete system.

Reason API bailed on UP1100 is they were overpriced for what you got. Sure 
it has a decent CPU, but NO memory bandwidth or decent capacity.

UP1500 looks MUCH better.

But API did not help much as they only brought in the 600MHz and not the 
700MHz. Samsung still sells them and they are readily available.

What I am seeing our customers ask for  this:
"Give us a machine like the LX was in it's time. Reasonably priced, fast, 
and flexible."

We should see that with the UP1500. Pity about the lack of UNIX but then 
this is becoming more irrelevant every day.


