On Fri, Apr 13, 2001 at 09:00:27PM +0400, Alexey Chupakhin wrote:

> Ha-ha, It seems, you compiling test by gcc on Alpha.
> GCC is very badly optimized for Alpha. If you try DEC/Compaq C, you just
> have a fantastic results.
> The rate for using gcc 2.95.2 and Compaq C  is about 10 times for Compaq C
> advantage.

Er, it's important to not exaggerate about this issue. I've never seen
a 10x difference. Compaq C *is* almost always better, but the
difference typically is in the 20% to 30% range. Occasionally it's
bigger, occasionally it's smaller.

He'd get a bigger boost from actually using 64 bit ints.

-- g




