correctly for at least *some* X stuff. It may be that the newer X video
drivers don't like the ISA version of the card. I've found as the hardware
gets more rare, drivers for it tend to follow the same path and start not to
work so hot. (I've seen the same thing with newer SRM releases running older
versions of Tru64/ Digital Unix)

Kurt

