Yeah, I searched and searched (archives, google, usenet, etc) and I
did see that thread. I've figured out a semi-half-ass work around; the
acient milo.ful will load a kernel as long as it is smaller then
700k. So I made a 2.2.19 kernel with the bare minimums that it will
boot. So I was able to at least get the install done. Now I need to
see if I can build a new kernel with networking support and keep it
under 700k...

If you still have your system, could you check the following? In ARCS
BIOS go to "Enter Setup" -> "Advanced Setup" -> "Show Firmware
Revision" and let me know what it says?

Thanks,
Ron - who wishes he understood what the the problem with ldmilo is...




